comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T13:18:18.456Z",codex-agent,"Design: reuse certified SDK readiness; rank priority then creation time then id; hold the shared repository lease across pick and claim/start. Compare declared active footprints plus actual merge-base diffs. Dry-run takes no write lease."
  "2026-10-16T13:23:45.767Z",codex-agent,"Focused integration suite: 11/11 pass, including default and custom agent selection, dependencies, direct parent filtering, own/foreign claims, unknown fallback, priority/age/id ordering and byte-identical dry-run fixture state. Use certified corpus ownership to avoid per-item read usage ledger writes during selection."
  "2026-10-16T13:26:24.563Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: changing only nextLane to omit active overlap exclusion made the regression choose the higher priority overlapping item; focused test exited 1 (0 pass, 1 fail). Restored implementation. Tests import TypeScript sources, so no dist rebuild was needed."
  "2026-10-16T13:57:28.933Z",codex-agent,"Final gates: npm run release:check and bun run release:check pass normally and with CI=1, isolated HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. Each run: 93/93 tests plus 1/1 packed npm/native Bun acceptance, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 21 authored source files at 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. Statements/lines 1337/1337; functions 72/72; branches 601/601 for normal npm and 600/600 for the other runs. Identity, types, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, production audit, package allowlist, changelog and publish attestation pass. Three behavioural revert proofs are recorded. Publication remains maintainer-gated."
